::MCR_U05_L04_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L04_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.2
Question:
In a table, 18 Grade 11 students prefer online review out of 30 Grade 11 students. What is P(online given Grade 11)?
{
=A. 18/30#Correct. Given Grade 11 restricts the denominator to the 30 Grade 11 students.
~B. 18/60#This uses the grand total, but the condition restricts the group.
~C. 30/18#This reverses the conditional probability ratio.
~D. 12/30#This uses the Grade 11 paper count, not the online count.
}
::MCR_U05_L04_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L04_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.2
Question:
In a table, 20 Grade 12 students prefer paper review out of 30 Grade 12 students. What is P(paper given Grade 12)?
{
~A. 20/60#This uses the grand total instead of the Grade 12 total.
=B. 20/30#Correct. The condition Grade 12 restricts the denominator to 30.
~C. 30/20#This reverses the ratio.
~D. 10/30#This is the Grade 12 online count, not paper.
}
::MCR_U05_L04_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L04_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.2
Question:
In a table, 18 Grade 11 students prefer online review and 28 total students prefer online review. What is P(Grade 11 given online)?
{
~A. 18/60#This uses the grand total instead of the online total.
~B. 28/18#This reverses the ratio.
=C. 18/28#Correct. Given online restricts the denominator to the 28 online students.
~D. 10/28#This uses the Grade 12 online count, not Grade 11 online.
}
::MCR_U05_L04_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L04_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.2
Question:
What does the word given usually tell you in a conditional probability question?
{
~A. Use the grand total every time#Given usually means the group is restricted, so the grand total may be wrong.
~B. Add the row and column totals#Adding totals does not identify the conditional denominator.
~C. Ignore the table#The table is needed to find the restricted count and total.
=D. Restrict the denominator to a smaller group#Correct. Given tells which group should be used as the denominator.
}
::MCR_U05_L04_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U05_L04_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.PR.2
Question:
A table shows 12 juniors play soccer out of 20 juniors. What is P(soccer given junior)?
{
~A. 8/20#This is the junior non-soccer count.
=B. 12/20#Correct. Given junior restricts the denominator to 20 juniors.
~C. 12/50#This uses a possible grand total instead of the restricted junior total.
~D. 20/12#This reverses the ratio.
}
